  "note": "Synthetic UTM wavy grid or seeded 50x50x10m scatter, 0.05m vertical offset. Ordinary production CPU C2C, same snapshots, spatial partitions, Morton query order, reference construction and worker counts. Await the already-started automatic CPU pool warm-up before any fixture/trial; its time is recorded separately and excluded. Five unmeasured full-sort/median-selection warm-up pairs precede alternating timed pairs. Times include planning, copies/transfers, tree builds, distances, joining and exact summaries; file load/rendering are excluded. Every timed pair must match displayed f32 distance bits and exact f64 statistics. Native builds/non-SIMD WASM remain scalar. CPU clocks, power and other applications are uncontrolled; no real-source or cross-machine speed claim. Only median calculation differs: sortedMillis uses full total_cmp sorting, selectedMillis selects the upper middle and (for even sizes) the maximum lower-partition value. The input reduction order and midpoint arithmetic are identical. Both CPU controls use scalar leaves and progressive joining; GPU controls use default prefetch, bounds, SIMD verification, batches and workgroups with reference/device reuse. GPU phase intervals exclude final summaries and can overlap; do not add them to infer wall time."
